# Blogs that answered the same search as another blog. Google
# indexes one page per intent and filed the other as "Crawled -
# currently not indexed". Merged into the stronger page; these 301s
# carry the old URL's signals to it. Specific rules must sit ABOVE
# the generic .html rule to match first, so they are prepended.

# Last rule (splats must follow every specific rule): any other /page.html -> /page as a PERMANENT 301. Without this rule the
# platform answers 307 (temporary), which tells Google to keep the .html URL.
/*.html  /:splat  301
